                <pb facs="0777" n="2159" xml:id="pg2159"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">751G.00/10–2254: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Secretary of State, at
                            Paris</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d1265-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret<lb/>niact</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-10-22T19:46:00-05:00">October 22, 1954—7:46
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Tedul 13. Personal for Secretary. From Acting
                    Secretary. I believe two subsequent telegrams on Viet-Nam<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d1265-f2"/> situation faithfully reflect your thinking. Telegram of
                    instructions to Heath and O’Daniel on starting limited MAAG program represents intensive week of work and
                    debate in OCB finally culminating in Defense and
                        JCS acceptance. This is significant step.
                    Whole matter presented to President this morning at NSC.<anchor n="3" xml:id="d1265-f3"/> He approved general lines of
                    action detailed by JCS and State in that
                    telegram. We now have something concrete to work with. It carries risk but
                    without some move we would remain on dead center.</p>
                <p>Suggest if possible you inform Deputy Defense Secretary Anderson of this message and instructions to
                        Heath and O’Daniel.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Hoover</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1265-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d1265-f1-content">
                <p>Drafted by Young of PSA.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1265-f2" n="2" xml:id="d1265-f2-content">
                <p>See Tedul 14 (1678 to Saigon), <ref
                        target="#d1266"><hi rendition="#italic">infra</hi></ref>, and telegram 1679
                    to Saigon (Tedul 15), <ref target="#pg2161">p.
                        2161</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d1265-f3" n="3" xml:id="d1265-f3-content">
                <p>See extracts from the memorandum of discussion at the 218th Meeting of the
                    National Security Council, Oct. 22, <ref target="#d1264"><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >supra</hi></ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
